# Local secrets for `pnpm dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (ignored by git) and
# `chmod 600 .dev.vars`. Names only here; never commit a value.
# See docs/security.md, "Secrets".
#
# These two are all a developer's machine needs. Everything else the Worker
# reads is a variable with a local value in wrangler.jsonc: an ENVIRONMENT of
# `development`, which trusts localhost and nothing else, Turnstile's published
# test site key, and a sender address that is never used, because locally no
# mail is sent. A line here that has one of those variables' names replaces its
# value on this machine; Wrangler ignores any other name.

# Signs session cookies. Any random value of 32 characters or more:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Turnstile's secret key. Locally, use Cloudflare's published test secret that
# passes every check. It is the same for everyone and is not a secret:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
#   1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# The platform console's owners (TS-099): addresses separated by commas. Each
# opens /platform after a code emailed to it. Empty closes the console.
PLATFORM_OWNERS=
